From ccabba5a9434778dcff67f5c6a897643ab05e9c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elsirion <elsirion@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:33:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agents): opt-in bubblewrap sandbox for local Linux agent
 launches
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a Linux-only "Sandbox local agents (bubblewrap)" switch under
Settings → Agents. When on, every locally launched TUI agent is wrapped
as `bwrap … -- /bin/sh -c '<command>'` at the PTY spawn seam, so the
host shell stays interactive while the agent and everything it spawns
run with a RAM-backed private home and /tmp, a read-only system, the
workspace (plus its git backend for worktrees) read-write, and the host
network shared.

Mounts and env follow workspacer's ~/.config/workspacer layout (env,
home_ro/, home_rw/, home_cow/) so existing configs work unchanged. Orca
adds what its own integration needs: ~/.orca/agent-hooks and the active
agent config dir (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / ~/.claude, CODEX_HOME / ~/.codex),
applied before user mounts so they can be overridden.

Missing bwrap or unusable user namespaces fail the launch with an
explicit error instead of running unsandboxed. Sandboxed launches count
as TUI customization so they never route to structured native chat.
SSH, WSL and ephemeral-VM hosts are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
