+- **Sandbox local agents (bubblewrap)** — Linux only. Wraps every locally launched agent in a [bubblewrap](https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap) sandbox: RAM-backed private home and `/tmp`, read-only system, the workspace (and its git backend) read-write, host network shared. Home mounts and extra env come from `~/.config/workspacer` (`env`, `home_ro/`, `home_rw/`, `home_cow/`, same layout as [workspacer](https://github.com/elsirion/workspacer)); Orca additionally binds its hook script directory and the active agent config dir. Requires `bwrap` and unprivileged user namespaces; a launch fails with an explicit error instead of running unsandboxed when either is missing. Sandboxed launches always open in the terminal, not the Chat UI. SSH, WSL, and Cloud VM targets are unaffected.
